Intercom project foundation

Workstream ID: ic-01
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/1
Status: DONE
Milestone: A resumable, documented, issue-backed project foundation
Dependencies: None

Purpose:
  Establish the development system without inventing a stack or claiming an app.
  Keep public engineering documentation separate from private session continuity.

Tasks:
  [x] Inspect repository, working tree, and existing tracking.
  [x] Adopt contributor rules and a repository-specific development manual.
  [x] Create numbered workstreams, index, product brief, and development ledger.
  [x] Register owned context continuity and publish a checked mesh refresh.
  [x] Create and verify dedicated Project, issues, statuses, and local backlinks.
  [x] Reconcile setup evidence and completion state.

Acceptance criteria:
  Documentation identifies the current product stage and unresolved decisions.
  Workstreams preserve all eight fields, stable IDs, and real dependencies.
  The owned private store is ignored by Git and discovered by Context Mesh.
  Each actual workstream has one issue and one item on the dedicated Project.
  Issue body/state, Project status, and local backlink agree with the workstream.
  No application stack, runtime, scheduler, commit, push, or deployment is added.

Completion evidence:
  Initial repository: README.md only; clean working tree at 68385a3.
  Authorized GitHub identity: Zanark; repository public with ADMIN permission.
  Baseline inventory: zero issues and no linked Project.
  Repository-specific manual, contributor rules, product brief, and ledger exist.
  Four TODO files retain all eight fields; seven local documentation links and
    two issue backlinks passed structural checks.
  git check-ignore confirms private continuity, local scratch, and .env exclusion.
  Checked Context Mesh build discovers Intercom as ctx-fd7ec571abba among 40
    contexts, publishes digest/index/dashboard, and reports no archived replies.
  Dedicated private Project: https://github.com/users/Zanark/projects/13.
  Independent remote read confirms #1 CLOSED/COMPLETED with Project Done;
    #2 OPEN with Project Todo. Both items contain the actual repository issues.
  Managed descriptions are mirrored from these public-safe workstream sources;
    final body baselines and read-back receipt live in docs/github-tracking.md.
  No application build or test suite exists; no runtime validation is claimed.
  Human acceptance and product implementation are not claimed.

Completion log:
  2026-11-10 - Owner requested new-project setup, context refresh, and manual adoption.
